{"name":"Confetti","hex":"#ddcb46","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"confetti","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Small pieces or strips (streamers) of colored paper or other material (metal, plaster, etc.) generally thrown about at festive occasions, especially at weddings and in victory celebrations.","Edible Italian sugarcoated almonds, especially those which are used as part of a traditional Italian wedding."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To scatter with confetti."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/confetti"}],"entries":[{"title":"Confetti","blocks":[{"text":"Confetti are small pieces or streamers of paper, mylar or metallic material, usually thrown at celebrations, especially parades and weddings. The origins are from the Latin confectum, with confetti the plural of Italian confetto, a small sweet. Modern paper confetti trace back to symbolic rituals of tossing grains and sweets during special occasions, traditional for numerous cultures throughout history as an ancient custom dating back to pagan times, but adapted from sweets and grains to paper through the centuries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Confetti_on_groom_at_Ash_Vale_%28Unsplash%29.jpg/330px-Confetti_on_groom_at_Ash_Vale_%28Unsplash%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Confetti"},{"title":"Confetti (Little Mix album)","blocks":[{"text":"Confetti is the sixth studio album by British girl group Little Mix, released on 6 November 2020 by RCA and Columbia Records. It was largely recorded before the COVID-19 pandemic, which interfered with the promotion plan for the album. Jesy Nelson announced her departure from the group in December 2020, a month after the album's release. Confetti is their first to be released under RCA Records, following their departure from Syco Music. Confetti is a pop and R&B record that lyrically addresses themes of self-acceptance, self-worth, freedom, and independence."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ab/Little_Mix_-_Confetti.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Confetti_(Little_Mix_album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Herzkonfetti.jpg/500px-Herzkonfetti.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Herzkonfetti.jpg/500px-Herzkonfetti.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A scattering of metallic confetti","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHerzkonfetti.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/2006_Rose_Bowl_post-game_celebration.jpg/500px-2006_Rose_Bowl_post-game_celebration.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/2006_Rose_Bowl_post-game_celebration.jpg/1280px-2006_Rose_Bowl_post-game_celebration.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/2006_Rose_Bowl_post-game_celebration.jpg/500px-2006_Rose_Bowl_post-game_celebration.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Confetti falls down on the Rose Bowl field after the victory of the Longhorns against the Trojans at the 2006 Rose Bowl, which was played on the 4 January 2006 (.mw-parser-output .tooltip-dotted{border-bottom:1px dotted;cursor:help}NCAA game), part of its post-game celebration","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2006_Rose_Bowl_post-game_celebration.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Amande-avolas-blanche.png/250px-Amande-avolas-blanche.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbn